{
  "id": "p31",
  "title": "The Last Edition",
  "titleZh": "最后一期",
  "topic": "地方周报停刊",
  "paragraphs": [
    [
      {
        "en": "My publisher runs a weekly paper with a regular staff.",
        "zh": "我的发行人经营一份周报，员工都很稳定。"
      },
      {
        "en": "I am the correspondent here, and I cover the mill.",
        "zh": "我是这里的记者，负责报道那家磨坊。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Our revenue is small, and our average print run falls.",
        "zh": "我们的收入很少，平均印量也在下滑。"
      },
      {
        "en": "A regular reader phones about a criminal case near the border.",
        "zh": "一位老读者打来电话，说边境附近有桩刑事案件。"
      },
      {
        "en": "The story involves a gang, a bar, and a stolen pack.",
        "zh": "这案子涉及一个团伙、一家酒吧，还有一包被偷的东西。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Then a senator calls, and her argument sounds extreme.",
        "zh": "接着一位参议员来电，她的论点听起来很极端。"
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "en": "The publisher announces a closure, and the whole staff is unable to speak.",
        "zh": "发行人宣布停刊，全体员工都说不出话来。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Suddenly a leak explains the failure, and the news is not acceptable.",
        "zh": "忽然一则泄密解释了这次失败，这消息让人无法接受。"
      },
      {
        "en": "We argue about the code, but the executive stays calm.",
        "zh": "我们为新闻准则争论，可那位主管始终镇定。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Our publisher is a homosexual man, and his partner owns a bookshop.",
        "zh": "我们的发行人是一位同性恋者，他的伴侣开着一家书店。"
      },
      {
        "en": "He tells the old myth of the founder with real expression.",
        "zh": "他讲起创办人的旧传说，神情真切。"
      },
      {
        "en": "A lord and a prince once wrote for this same tiny paper.",
        "zh": "一位勋爵和一位王子都曾为这份小报写过稿。"
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "en": "Our farewell ceremony fills the mill on a cold evening.",
        "zh": "一个寒冷的晚上，我们的告别仪式挤满了磨坊。"
      },
      {
        "en": "A minister speaks, and a player from the local team listens.",
        "zh": "一位部长讲话，本地球队的一名球员在听。"
      },
      {
        "en": "People chat and wipe their eyes, and the mood is warm.",
        "zh": "人们聊着，擦着眼泪，气氛温暖。"
      },
      {
        "en": "The executive announces his retirement, and the crowd claps.",
        "zh": "主管宣布退休，人群鼓起掌来。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Our mutual respect is a real asset, and it will not vanish.",
        "zh": "我们彼此的尊重是真正的财富，不会消失。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Then he praises our unique and lasting connection to the town.",
        "zh": "接着他称赞我们与这座小镇独特而持久的联系。"
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "en": "My desk is quiet, and commerce shows a clear trend.",
        "zh": "我的桌子安静下来，商业也显出清晰的趋势。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Our last issue will instruct readers and spur a debate.",
        "zh": "我们最后一期将给读者以教益，也激起一场讨论。"
      },
      {
        "en": "A complaint about a superior officer reaches the desk.",
        "zh": "一封投诉上级军官的信送到了桌上。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Therefore we print it, and a few readers complain.",
        "zh": "于是我们把它登出来，少数读者开始抱怨。"
      },
      {
        "en": "My final script is impressive, and the design is clean.",
        "zh": "我最后一篇稿子很出色，版面也干净。"
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "en": "Later a jury hears the conflict, and the arrival is tense.",
        "zh": "后来陪审团审理这场冲突，到场时气氛紧张。"
      },
      {
        "en": "A maker of church music relates religion to daily life.",
        "zh": "一位教堂音乐创作者把宗教与日常生活联系起来。"
      },
      {
        "en": "My salary is modest, and my deposit is small.",
        "zh": "我的薪水不高，存款也少。"
      },
      {
        "en": "The town deserves better, and the paper was a super friend.",
        "zh": "这座小镇值得更好的，而这份报纸曾是个极好的朋友。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Its end is inevitable, but our desperate hope remains.",
        "zh": "它的终结不可避免，但我们仍抱着迫切的希望。"
      }
    ]
  ],
